MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The stainless fasteners fit my repeated interest in assembling and repairing things, and the lag bolt assortment is especially useful because it includes several lengths and washers.",
    "The glue fits alongside my tapes and epoxy for joining materials, while disposable gloves could support that messy work if they are suitable for the substances involved."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The printer filaments require a printing project I have not shown a need for; different colors and finishes do not make them useful for my current fastening and repair work.",
    "The breadboards are for building electronic circuits, which does not follow from my use of inspection tools, measuring instruments, and mechanical fasteners."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Having an interest in making and repairing things seems to have been stretched into an interest in 3D printing supplies.",
    "My use of technical tools seems to have been treated as a reason to offer electronics prototyping supplies, even though those tools serve different tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, rivet nuts, bolts, and other fasteners suggest that practical joining and assembly needs matter more to me right now than a broad connection to DIY activities.",
    "Exact dimensions and head styles affect whether I need a fastener now: the small pan head screws look useful, while I would wait for a specific need before choosing the larger flat head screws."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my need for repair and fastening supplies but extended that interest too far into printing and circuit building."
}
